    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **33 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for `POST /api/owners`: the response now carries `bulkSignupWarning: true` when more than 80 owners had already been created for the request's registration day at the moment of creation, and `false` otherwise. The value is a snapshot captured at create time (like `namesakeCount`), so it reads back consistently via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges, following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md:\n\n1. **New pipeline function** `AssignBulkSignupWarning.java` \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the built owner's business day (the same accumulation path as `RequireDailyOwnerLimit`) and sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. It runs after `BuildOwner` (so the registration date is set) and before `SaveOwner` (so the count excludes the owner being created).\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `bulkWarning` step between `assignMembership` and `save`, with `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly, required) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and MapStruct auto-maps it.\n\n5. **Schema SQL** \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column to all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\nNote: the warning band is 81\u201399 owners/day; at 100 the create is already rejected 429 by the existing `RequireDailyOwnerLimit` rule (`DAILY_LIMIT = 100`), which is consistent with a \"warning before the hard cap\" reading of the spec.",
